WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.101
<v Examiner>Four marks.

2
00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:04.802
<v Examiner>Explain the role of emotional intelligence,

3
00:00:04.802 --> 00:00:09.325
<v Examiner>and discuss its impact on therapeutic communication in nursing practice.

4
00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:14.832
This is Lisa's own practice question, so here's her model answer, close to word for word,

5
00:00:14.832 --> 00:00:16.537
with the structure she taught.

6
00:00:16.987 --> 00:00:17.930
Explain first.

7
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:21.363
Emotional intelligence is the ability to recognise,

8
00:00:21.363 --> 00:00:26.816
understand and manage your own emotions while responding appropriately to others.

9
00:00:26.816 --> 00:00:30.518
It lets nurses respond compassionately and build trust.

10
00:00:30.518 --> 00:00:35.769
Its key components, in her order: self-awareness, self-regulation, motivation,

11
00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:37.519
empathy and social skills.

12
00:00:37.519 --> 00:00:43.443
Self-regulation means keeping your natural reaction concealed so the patient feels safe.

13
00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:46.270
Motivation is internal, not about rewards.

14
00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:51.117
Empathy is feeling with the person, not just recognising what they feel.

15
00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:55.695
Social skills are things like conflict management and collaboration.

16
00:00:56.145 --> 00:00:58.042
Now discuss, the bigger part.

17
00:00:58.042 --> 00:01:03.931
In nursing, emotional intelligence supports therapeutic communication by enabling empathy,

18
00:01:03.931 --> 00:01:06.548
self-awareness and emotional regulation.

19
00:01:06.548 --> 00:01:08.249
Its impact is significant.

20
00:01:08.249 --> 00:01:11.063
It improves the nurse-patient relationship,

21
00:01:11.063 --> 00:01:16.625
helps the nurse understand what the patient needs, and supports patient-centred care.

22
00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:21.008
It also helps manage challenging interactions and reduces conflict.

23
00:01:21.008 --> 00:01:23.495
Overall, it strengthens communication,

24
00:01:23.495 --> 00:01:28.729
leading to better patient outcomes and more effective therapeutic relationships.

25
00:01:29.179 --> 00:01:33.457
How it links to therapeutic use of self, in case that's the wording.

26
00:01:33.457 --> 00:01:37.106
Therapeutic use of self means using your personal insight,

27
00:01:37.106 --> 00:01:42.139
presence and authenticity to build trust, including acknowledging your own bias.

28
00:01:42.139 --> 00:01:46.857
It rests on two things, and the lecturers' practice quiz asks exactly this:

29
00:01:46.857 --> 00:01:50.129
competent communication, and emotional intelligence.

30
00:01:50.579 --> 00:01:52.844
Emotional intelligence: recognise,

31
00:01:52.844 --> 00:01:57.307
understand and manage your own emotions while responding to others.

32
00:01:57.307 --> 00:02:01.838
Self-awareness, self-regulation, motivation, empathy, social skills.

33
00:02:01.838 --> 00:02:07.234
Impact: empathy, trust, understanding needs, patient-centred care, less conflict,

34
00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:08.300
better outcomes.

35
00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:13.896
Therapeutic use of self rests on competent communication and emotional intelligence.
